  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 180554\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n800 PM HST Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nWestern East Pacific (EP98):\nShowers and thunderstorms associated with a broad area of low\npressure located well southwest of the southern tip of the Baja\nCalifornia Peninsula remain disorganized. Environmental conditions\nappear conducive for additional development of this system, and a\ntropical depression is likely to form this weekend as it moves\nwestward at 10 to 15 mph across the western East Pacific.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...medium...60 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...80 percent.\n\nWell East-Southeast of the Hawaiian Islands (Former TD15-E):\nShowers and thunderstorms associated with the remnants of Tropical\nDepression Fifteen-E remain limited. Environmental conditions appear\nconducive for some development of this system as it moves gradually\nwestward to west-southwestward, remaining well east-southeast to\nsoutheast of the Hawaiian Islands.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...10 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...30 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Pierce/Evans/Gibbs\nNNNN",
